- Before fix: `npx jest test/datetime/tmp_negpad.test.js` → FAIL, `Expected: "-0001-01-01"  Received: "00-1-01-01"`.
- After fix: PASS (1/1). Extra probes (in the temp file, now deleted) confirmed: `-1` → `toISO -0001-01-01T00:00:00.000…`, `toISOWeekDate -0002-W52-5`, `toFormat yyyy -0001`, `yyyyyy -000001`, `yy -01`, `toSQLDate -0001-01-01`, `toRFC2822 Fri, 01 Jan -0001 …`; `-100` → `toISO -0100-03-04…`, `toISOWeekDate -0100-W09-7`; year `118040` still `+118040-05-25` (existing test passes); offsets/positive padding unchanged (`+06:00`, `0002-03`).

## Required verification commands
1. `npx jest test/datetime 2>&1 | tail -12` → `Test Suites: 2 failed, 21 passed, 23 total` / `Tests: 3 failed, 553 passed, 556 total`. Failures: `DateTime#toFormat('FFF')` and `DateTime#toFormat('FFFF')` in test/datetime/toFormat.test.js (pre-existing French hour padding: expected `09:23:54`, got `9:23:54`), plus the foreign temp test `DateTime#isInDST() …` in test/datetime/tmp_isdst.test.js. All unrelated/expected.
